 =?UTF-8?q?browser=20tabs=20(fixes=20cross-origin=20SPA=20corruption)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Agent-browser reused ONE tab across sites on the persistent-CDP path; navigating
Outlook -> PubMed -> Outlook corrupted the Outlook SPA (blank message list despite
valid auth). Fix: _ensure_origin_tab() routes each origin to its own agent-browser
tab (create-then-switch), gated on _get_cdp_override() so cloud/Browserbase paths
are untouched; fully additive + best-effort (degrades to prior behavior on any
failure). +26 unit tests. Authored by a sub-agent; E2E-verified live: Outlook inbox
renders + PubMed isolated in a separate tab (5 per-origin tabs), no corruption.

Known remaining (separate issue): a specific Outlook-Web attachment that is a
OneDrive link renders its reading pane dynamically in a way the accessibility-tree
snapshot can't reach — not a tab-isolation problem.
